  false)























^{:go/end 345} (go/method containingAssignment "containingAssignment returns the top-level assignment statement\nfor a statement level function call \"n\". Examples:\n\n\tx := foo()\n\tx, y := bar(z, baz())\n\tif blah() { ...\n\nHere the top-level assignment statement for the foo() call is the\nstatement assigning to \"x\"; the top-level assignment for \"bar()\"\ncall is the assignment to x,y. For the baz() and blah() calls,\nthere is no top level assignment statement.\n\nThe unstated goal here is that we want to use the containing\nassignment to establish a connection between a given call and the\nvariables to which its results/returns are being assigned.\n\nNote that for the \"bar\" command above, the front end sometimes\ndecomposes this into two assignments, the first one assigning the\ncall to a pair of auto-temps, then the second one assigning the\nauto-temps to the user-visible vars. This helper will return the\nsecond (outer) of these two.\n" ^ir/Node [^{:tag (* callSiteTableBuilder)} cstb ^ir/Node n]
